<div id="A2.SS6.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">JailbreakBench.</span>
Table <a href="#A2.T11" title="Table 11 ‣ B.6 Attack Success Rate by Risk Categories ‣ Appendix B ARMs Experiment Details and Additional Results ‣ ARMs: Adaptive Red-Teaming Agent against Multimodal Models with Plug-and-Play Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a> show the attack results on JailbreakBench evaluation by 10 risk categories.
Abbreviations used in the table headers are as follows: “DIS” is “Disinformation”; “EH” is “Economic harm”; “EA” is “Expert advice”; “FD” is “Fraud/Deception”; “GDM” is “Government decision-making”; “HD” is “Harassment/Discrimination”; “MH” is “Malware/Hacking”; “PH” is “Physical harm”; “PRIV” is “Privacy”; and “SAC” is “Sexual/Adult content”.</p>
</div>
