<div id="A2.SS6.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS6.p5.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS6.p5.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EU-AI-Act.</span>
Table <a href="#A2.T13" title="Table 13 ‣ B.6 Attack Success Rate by Risk Categories ‣ Appendix B ARMs Experiment Details and Additional Results ‣ ARMs: Adaptive Red-Teaming Agent against Multimodal Models with Plug-and-Play Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> show the attack results on EU AI Act evaluation by 13 risk categories.
Abbreviations used in the table headers are as follows: “AD” is “Automated Discrimination”; “AO” is “Automated Operation”; “BC” is “Biometric Categorization”; “BIC” is “Biometric Information Collection”; “DI” is “Deceptive Interfaces”; “EM” is “Emotion Manipulation”; “HAR” is “Harassment”; “HTC” is “Hate/Toxic Content”; “PJ” is “Predictive Justice”; “SS” is “Social Scoring”; “SM” is “Subliminal Manipulation”; “SYS” is “System Security”; and “VE” is “Vulnerability Exploitation”.</p>
</div>
