<div id="A3.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A3.SS2.p4.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A3.SS2.p4.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">EU-AI-Act.</span>
Table <a href="#A3.T26" title="Table 26 ‣ C.2 Safety Benchmark Evaluation with ARMs-Bench ‣ Appendix C ARMs-Bench Details ‣ ARMs: Adaptive Red-Teaming Agent against Multimodal Models with Plug-and-Play Attacks" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">26</span></a> show the attack results on EU AI Act evaluation by 13 risk categories.
Abbreviations used in the table headers are as follows: “AD” is “Automated Discrimination”; “AO” is “Automated Operation”; “BC” is “Biometric Categorization”; “BIC” is “Biometric Information Collection”; “DI” is “Deceptive Interfaces”; “EM” is “Emotion Manipulation”; “HAR” is “Harassment”; “HTC” is “Hate/Toxic Content”; “PJ” is “Predictive Justice”; “SS” is “Social Scoring”; “SM” is “Subliminal Manipulation”; “SYS” is “System Security”; and “VE” is “Vulnerability Exploitation”.</p>
</div>
